CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 11
Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to appropriate, comfortable, and needs-based complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and
j. to receive continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

Article 2
The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence are: a. to prevent all forms of violence against women and children; b. to provide protection and services to women and children victims of gender-based violence;
c. to provide a sense of security to women and children victims of violence; d. to restore the physical, psychological and economic condition of women and children victims of violence;
e. the best interests of women and children victims of violence that occurs in the domestic and/or public sphere; and
f. to provide certainty of assistance to victims in the legal process against perpetrators of violence against women and children.

